/T (The Castellammarese War was not simply a conflict between two rival bosses, but a struggle that changed the balance of power inside organized crime entirely. Old traditions began clashing with a younger generation focused more on profit, expansion, and long-term control. Some mafiosi relied on loyalty and fear, others relied on strategy, diplomacy, business, and connections. Throughout the war, crews disappeared, betrayals became common, and neutrality slowly became impossible.)
