/Title (New York in 1930 was not controlled only by politicians or the police. Behind restaurants, gambling clubs, docks, and speakeasies, Mafia factions were fighting for territory, money, influence, and survival while Prohibition flooded the underworld with more profit than ever before. Alliances shifted constantly, rumors spread faster than bullets, and even the most powerful bosses in the city were never completely safe.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1115 0 R
/Next 1120 0 R
>>
