1153 0 obj
<<
/Title (Bootlegging quickly became one of the most lucrative illegal industries in the country. Criminal groups took control of the production, smuggling, and sale of alcohol, often working through networks of speakeasies, corrupt officials, and transportation routes that stretched across cities and states. In New York City, this system became especially complex due to its size, population, and importance as a commercial hub. Organized crime figures were able to accumulate significant wealth in a short period of time, which they reinvested into expanding their operations, recruiting members, and securing influence over both legal and illegal institutions.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1157 0 R
/Next 1151 0 R
>>
